nd the  religious zealotry of his followers has  started to get out of hand now you might  be asking yourself why aren't muadeeb  and chani married well in an effort to  ease tensions within the various houses  of the empire mouri marries princess  ireland carino the daughter of former  emperor shaddam it seems to be a  marriage entitle only as muadeeb's real  love has always been chaney one of the  main antagonists of children of dune is  princess winsocya currino daughter of  emperor shadom and his sister ireland  her father's grip on the empire is no  more and her house has effectively lost  most of its power so she devises a plan  to undermine paul by creating what's  called a gola of his old friend duncan  idaho who died in the original dune a  gola is an artificially created human  almost like a clone but a gola can  possess memories of the past the hope  here is that this gola can be  manipulated to assassinate paul at the  same time multiple plots against muadib  and his family make life on dune a  dangerous affair we find out someone has  been poisoning chani so that she can't  conceive princess when cecilia has  stolen a sand worm in an attempt to make  spice on her own planet of seleusa  secundus and a terrorist attack against  muadib leaves him blinded but even  though he is blinded he is still able to  see with his powers they blinded my body  but not my vision for their own safety  muadeeb takes chany who was able to  conceive to the safety of the desert  there she gives birth to twins but dies  in the process at this point muadeeb who  had meddled in what he called impossible  futures still ends up in a scenario  where the woman he loves dies so he goes  off into the desert to die alone it is  only then that he considers himself  truly free but that's not where the  story ends in fact the majority of  children of dune revolves around paul's  two children lato the second named after  the duke and gonima the story advances  several years with lado just six months  away from being of age to take control  of the empire since then their aunt alia  who you may remember as the blue-eyed  girl from the original dune has been  holding power as regent she ended up  orchestrating the death of the reverend  mother moaim and the guild navigator  edric right around the time of muadeeb's  disappearance but since then a lot has  changed alia has grown a cult of  personality around herself and the  rituals and myths surrounding muhaddib  have become perverted she has turned  much of arrakis's spice sands into green  pastures limiting the amount of spice  production and thus driving up demand it  has gotten so bad that a rebel group of  fremen have challenged alia's powers  which could turn the entire planet into  an all-out civil war and to make matters  worse alia has turned abomination in the  dune universe this refers to when one  becomes psychologically unstable and  this manifests in alia when she is  haunted by voices particularly that of  her grandfather vladimir harkinan i  don't think this is mentioned in the  1984 version but lady jessica is the  illegitimate daughter of vladimir  harkinan making alia his granddaughter  speaking of lady jessica she returns to  arrakis after years off planet doomed to  her brings back too many painful  memories after all both her husband and  son died there this has caused  resentment in alia who feels her mother  abandoned her you mix all this together  along with some assassination attempts  and alia becomes much like a mad king  ordering extermination of various  feminine rebel groups and building  suspicion that her niece and nephew may  usurp her power we're also introduced to  a character known as the preacher which  the mini-series does a very bad job of  hiding the fact that he is actually  muadeeb returned he isn't too happy how  his name has been used to justify a lot  of the bad [ __ ] going on and with things  hitting a fever pitch lady jessica  denounces alia in front of the people  and another assassination attempt occurs  which causes complete pandemonium  throughout the palace lato and ganyman  make it to the desert where they are  chased down by two laza tigers sent by  princess wencesia this is all part of  the princess's plan to regain control of  the empire if the tradies twins are  killed and alias it comes to madness she  may have a shot of regaining power lado  however fakes his death and his sister  believes him to have died by one of  these tigers this is all part of lato's  plan to follow what is known as the  golden path by following the golden path  lato could prevent humanity's own  destruction for paul the path was so  arduous that he left it to live alone in  the desert because he could see the  future he knew the drastic measures he  would have had to take in order for  humanity to avoid annihilation and that  was just too much for him his son lato  on the other hand embraced the golden  path on his journey he stumbles upon a  smuggler's den where san trout are sold  off world to the highest bidder santrout  are basically baby sand worms who over  the course of thousands of years turn  into these giant sandworms we see on  dune lado ends up allowing the sand  worms to attach themselves to his body  which begins a process of transformation  affording him super human-like abilities  even greater than what he already has  this gives him super speed agility and  strength alia believing her nephew to be  dead and with enemies around her at  every turn agrees to a political  marriage of convenience between ganima  and princess winsosya's son faradan this  was an arrangement designed behind  alia's back by duncan idaho in the book  these two are married but the  mini-series portrays them as lovers  duncan will later kill alia's lover  javid in the neutral territory of  sichthabar essentially forcing stilgar  who up to this point was neutral to join  the war against alia you see once ali  would find out her lover was killed on  this neutral territory she'd attack  stilgar's fremen tribe in retaliation at  the same time lato finds his father in  the desert up until this point he had  only seen his father in dreams lato  tells him he wishes to make a future  free of one man's vision free of a  future that is predetermined and he  hopes with himself at the helm he can do  this so he ventures back to era keen to  seize control from his crazy aunt at the  capitol princess winsocia arrives with  her son for the marriage between him and  ganyman ganima earlier told ireland that  she hates this marriage and will kill  faradan on their wedding night but  something completely unexpected happens  here something the mini-series doesn't  do a particularly good job at probably  because they simply didn't have enough  time faraday betrays his mother and  openly tells him that it was his mom who  was responsible for assassinating lato  remember they still think he died from  that tiger this betrayal was spurred by  years of abuse ferran received from his  mother who thought he was weak and would  never be a man it's only after this  betrayal and the princess is banished  that she finally sees him as a man  you're more of a man than i ever thought  possible fraud tells ganima this is her  wedding present how cute muadeeb returns  to arakin and causes a stir as a crowd  forms around him he believes that one  blasphemy remains and that is alia  sensing this preacher is her brother  alia hides herself among the crowd only  to be discovered by him it's only a  brief moment before a fremen assassin  kills muadeeb later arrives and holds  his father in his hands as the two  disappear into the sand we then  awkwardly transition to the wedding  which seems to be going on even after  this big event lato interrupts the  service to put an end to alia once and  for all to reach humanity of the  perversions done in wardeeb's name  and to save it from the abomination  known as aliyah we get to see lato's  proficiency in the weirding way this  close hand-to-hand comet that allows him  to teleport around and make quick work  of alia's guards aliyah then joins the  fight but isn't strong enough to take  down her nephew he ultimately gives her  the opportunity to kill him as the voice  of baron harkin yells at her to finish  him but aliyah breaks free of these  voices and ultimately chooses to kill  herself thus ending her reign of terror  lady jessica leaves dune while gurney  and ireland stay lato returns to stilgar  with alia's water and asks him to spread  it among the sand think of it as the  fremen way of spreading ashes he also  gives him his father's signet ring that  once belonged to both paul and lato the  first it's a sign that all humans make  mistakes not mentioned in the  mini-series but lato ends up as emperor  marrying his sister to consolidate power  but this is purely a political move and  the two never consummate their marriage  ganima ends up having children with  feron her concubine that's where the  children of dune mini-series ends  however there are three more novels  after this but as far as i know no big  budget shows or films that cover them  i'm hoping to cover the new dune movie  when it hits theaters later this month  so be sure to like and subscribe and  stick around for that thanks for  watching everyone for more bad takes you  can follow me on twitter and instagram  at thinkstoryyt until next time remember  daddy loves you very much  [Music]

